Video-mode variant of the jd35695 panel (UNTested: B's battery died before a
clean test — s179/s180 boot attempts all hit the discharged battery).
Apply on top of the cmd-mode driver + op2-display.dtsi to try video mode:
it should remove tearing (panel syncs on HSYNC/VSYNC) and allow 60 fps
(continuous HS stream instead of one slow cmd-mode transfer per commit).

--- a/kernel/panel/panel-oneplus2-jd35695.c
+++ b/kernel/panel/panel-oneplus2-jd35695.c
@@ -286,8 +286,7 @@
-	dsi->mode_flags = MIPI_DSI_MODE_VIDEO_BURST | MIPI_DSI_MODE_VIDEO_HSE |
-			  MIPI_DSI_CLOCK_NON_CONTINUOUS;
+	dsi->mode_flags = MIPI_DSI_MODE_VIDEO | MIPI_DSI_MODE_VIDEO_SYNC_PULSE;

--- a/kernel/dts/op2-display.dtsi
+++ b/kernel/dts/op2-display.dtsi
@@ panel@0: add before the port subnode, after all properties:
+				/* stock jd35695 1080p60 timing (h 1080+100+8+82,
+				 * v 1920+3+2+7), needed in video mode for HSYNC/VSYNC */
+				display-timings {
+					timing@0 {
+						clock-frequency = <147218000>;
+						hactive = <1080>;
+						hfront-porch = <100>;
+						hback-porch = <82>;
+						hsync-len = <8>;
+						vactive = <1920>;
+						vfront-porch = <3>;
+						vback-porch = <7>;
+						vsync-len = <2>;
+						hsync-active-high;
+						vsync-active-high;
+						de-active-high;
+						pixelclk-active-high;
+					};
+				};
